count</b>. An investment still under contract is settled first, as your agreement says; then we delete your account and email you. <b class="gd-ui">Keep my account</b> withdraws the request. Agreements, statements and tax records are kept as the law requires.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="profile-and-notices-your-name-and-password-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your name and password (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Profile. <b class="gd-ui">Save my display name</b> changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press <b class="gd-ui">Request a name change</b>, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b> sends you to the password page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="profile-and-notices-choose-your-notifications-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Choose your notifications (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b>, under <b class="gd-ui">Notification preferences</b>, lists each kind of notification we send you, with a switch for <b class="gd-ui">Push</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. A switch is saved the moment you move it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How often</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Instant</b> sends each one as it happens. <b class="gd-ui">Daily summary</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary</b> holds the optional emails and sends them as one email in the morning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quiet hours</b>: turn them on and set the times. Optional phone alerts and texts wait until the quiet hours end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn every optional notification off</b> stops them all at once. You still see every message in your portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The kinds under <b class="gd-ui">Always on</b> cannot be switched off: security and sign-in codes, legal and agreement notices, statements and payments.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">If a text cannot be sent, the same message comes by email instead, so nothing is lost.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'content-calendar', 'chapter', 'marketing-on-facebook-marketplace', null, 'Content calendar', 'The month of social posts: approve, edit, reject or regenerate each before it is published.',
  '**Marketing** > **Content calendar** shows the month of social posts for the Facebook Page, Instagram and TikTok. Sales, customer service and Fleet can use it. Nothing is published until one of you approves it.

## Read the month

1. The calendar is written by itself near the end of the month before. Each post has a format (reel, carousel, photo or story), a content pillar, an opening line, a caption, hashtags, the best time for each channel and a music suggestion.
2. From tablet width the month shows as a grid. Tap a post in the grid to jump to it. On a phone you get the list.
3. **To approve**, **Approved**, **Posted** and **Rejected** filter the list.
4. If a month is empty, press **Write the calendar**.

## Approve, edit, reject or regenerate

1. **Approve** schedules the post at its best time on each channel. For a reel, choose the short video first. Make one from the car''s photos on the queue page if there is none.
2. **Edit** changes the opening line, the caption, the hashtags, the day or the music.
3. **Regenerate** writes the post again with other words or another car.
4. **Reject** asks why. A rejected post is never published. **Restore** brings it back.
5. **Take the approval back** cancels the scheduled posts and makes it a draft again.

## Publishing

1. With Meta connected, approved photos and reels post to the Facebook Page and Instagram by themselves at their time.
2. Stories, carousels and every TikTok post are posted by hand. So is everything while Meta is not connected. When one is due you get an alert: open the queue, download it, post it with the caption and the music, then paste the post''s link under **Posted by hand**.
3. Music is a suggestion. The apps do not let us attach their licensed sounds, so pick the sound when you post.
4. Comments and direct messages get the same AI replies as texts and chat: few, marked as AI, basic questions only. Anything else goes to a person.

## Results

1. Posts that Meta published get their views, likes, comments, shares and saves by themselves.
2. For a post made by hand, press **Add results** on the post and type the numbers from the app.
3. The next month''s calendar leans on what did best: the pillar, the format and the hour.',
  '<p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Content calendar</b> shows the month of social posts for the Facebook Page, Instagram and TikTok. Sales, customer service and Fleet can use it. Nothing is published until one of you approves it.</p><section class="gd-task" id="content-calendar-read-the-month" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read the month</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The calendar is written by itself near the end of the month before. Each post has a format (reel, carousel, photo or story), a content pillar, an opening line, a caption, hashtags, the best time for each channel and a music suggestion.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">From tablet width the month shows as a grid. Tap a post in the grid to jump to it. On a phone you get the list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">To approve</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approved</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Rejected</b> filter the list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">If a month is empty, press <b class="gd-ui">Write the calendar</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="content-calendar-approve-edit-reject-or-regenerate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve, edit, reject or regenerate</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> schedules the post at its best time on each channel. For a reel, choose the short video first. Make one from the car&#39;s photos on the queue page if there is none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> changes the opening line, the caption, the hashtags, the day or the music.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Regenerate</b> writes the post again with other words or another car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Reject</b> asks why. A rejected post is never published. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> brings it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Take the approval back</b> cancels the scheduled posts and makes it a draft again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="content-calendar-publishing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publishing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">With Meta connected, approved photos and reels post to the Facebook Page and Instagram by themselves at their time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Stories, carousels and every TikTok post are posted by hand. So is everything while Meta is not connected. When one is due you get an alert: open the queue, download it, post it with the caption and the music, then paste the post&#39;s link under <b class="gd-ui">Posted by hand</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Music is a suggestion. The apps do not let us attach their licensed sounds, so pick the sound when you post.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Comments and direct messages get the same AI replies as texts and chat: few, marked as AI, basic questions only. Anything else goes to a person.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="content-calendar-results" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Results</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Posts that Meta published get their views, likes, comments, shares and saves by themselves.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">For a post made by hand, press <b class="gd-ui">Add results</b> on the post and type the numbers from the app.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The next month&#39;s calendar leans on what did best: the pillar, the format and the hour.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'shared-tools', 'chapter', 'car-maintenance', 'Every function has the calendar and Find a renter. Use them to answer questions fast.

## Which cars are free (release 44)

At the top of **Calendar**: choose the **Pickup** and the **Return** the customer wants and you see every car at once.

1. Each car says **Available** (green edge) or **Not available** (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the **Next free** start for the same length of rental.
2. An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.
3. Narrow it with **Class**, **Seats at least** and **Price a day up to**, or tick **Available only**.
4. Customer service and Sales: press **Offer these dates** on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.
5. No customer''s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.

## The calendar

1. Every car with its photo, its bookings, requests and blocks, in the colours of the legend above it: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance, block. The red line is now. Tap a bar for its details; on a phone it opens on the agenda, by day.
2. Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by plate, booking or name.
3. Fleet and customer service can remove a cleaning block from its side panel (**Remove the block**) when a car is ready sooner.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 800; address: carmacars.ca/va/calendar; pins: 1 60.2 33.8, 2 28.5 17.5")

## Find a car

**Bookings**, the **Find a car** tab. A renter quotes the car code on the car''s page (like CC-7F3A).

1. Type the car code, a plate, a VIN or the name. Each car shows its code, plate, status and its page on the site.
2. In Add a rental, type the car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.

## Find a renter

1. Search by name, email, phone or booking number.
2. Opening a renter''s private details asks for a reason (**Open with a reason**). It is kept in the access log.
3. The renter''s record has **Add a note** and the **Activity** log: everything about the renter, newest first, with a chip per type (All by default), **Search the activity**, **Older** for the next 50, and **Email**, **Call** and **Text**. Fleet does not see payments in it.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-07-renters-desktop-99cfd0ef.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 240; address: carmacars.ca/va/renters; pins: 1 68.3 34.6")

## Email the renter

Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance can all write to the renter from a booking: press **Email the renter**, or open the **Messages & history** section.

The booking page, the car page and the listing review are the same pages an Admin opens. The car page has the Admin''s tabs your function uses: **Overview**, **Rates & fees** and **Maintenance** (Fleet), **Listing** and **Documents**; an old link to a car''s maintenance opens its Maintenance tab. You see the sections and buttons of your function: Finance has the money, the refunds and the deposit; Fleet the field jobs, the handovers and the car''s rates; customer service the review and offer, changes and extensions; Sales the requests and offers.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from.
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars and the renter can answer in their account; the answer opens a task for customer service.
3. On a booking an insurer pays you can choose Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance) as the sender, and **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster on the booking.

The form is under the booking''s Activity log (release 35), which lists the messages both ways, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes and the rest, newest first, with a chip per type and a search. Each email counts against the daily email limit, shown under the form with today''s number.

### Find a booking
**Bookings**: type at least 3 characters of the booking number (CC-1042, 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number, a plate or a car code, then press Enter. **My bookings** lists yours, with your commission. Every search is logged, as Find a renter.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer for new requests, replies to answer and urgent problems, even with the portal closed.

1. Open **Profile** (top of the menu). Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications. The first page of the portal also offers it once.
2. Under **What to alert me about**: new requests, booking changes and messages are on for staff; payments are off until you tick them.
3. **Send a test alert** checks the device. **Remove** takes an old phone off.

On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**). Use your phone''s own Focus or Do Not Disturb for quiet hours.

### Search

The **Search** button at the top of every page (or press **/** where the page has no search box of its own) finds pages and the records your role may open: bookings and requests by number, renter name, email, phone or plate, renters, owners and cars.

### A VIN from the car

VIN fields have **Scan the barcode** (the barcode in the driver''s door frame or under the windshield) and **Photo of the VIN**. Check what was read against the car before saving.

## Alerts by email

Alerts that are not urgent come together in one email at most once an hour; urgent ones (a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, the site down) still come on their own. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once. Choose on **Profile**, Notifications: alerts by email, **Change how often**: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.

> Tip: To change the email you sign in with, open Profile, Sign-in and press **Change my email**: type the new address, and we send a confirmation link to it and tell the old address. Your email changes only when the link is opened, and every record of yours follows it.', 'Shared tools', 'The calendar and Find a renter.',
