 car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Opening a renter&#39;s private details asks for a reason (<b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>). It is kept in the access log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter&#39;s record has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, with a chip per type (All by default), <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> for the next 50, and <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. Fleet does not see payments in it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/renters</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/240"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-07-renters-desktop-99cfd0ef.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="240"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.3%;top:34.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-email-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance can all write to the renter from a booking: press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>, or open the <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section.</p><p class="gd-p">The booking page, the car page and the listing review are the same pages an Admin opens. The car page has the Admin&#39;s tabs your function uses: <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> (Fleet), <b class="gd-ui">Listing</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>; an old link to a car&#39;s maintenance opens its Maintenance tab. You see the sections and buttons of your function: Finance has the money, the refunds and the deposit; Fleet the field jobs, the handovers and the car&#39;s rates; customer service the review and offer, changes and extensions; Sales the requests and offers.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Write a <b class="gd-ui">Subject</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Message</b>, or pick a <b class="gd-ui">Quick reply</b> to start from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>. It goes from CarmaCars and the renter can answer in their account; the answer opens a task for customer service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking an insurer pays you can choose Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance) as the sender, and <b class="gd-ui">Email the adjuster</b> writes to the adjuster on the booking.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The form is under the booking&#39;s Activity log (release 35), which lists the messages both ways, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes and the rest, newest first, with a chip per type and a search. Each email counts against the daily email limit, shown under the form with today&#39;s number.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Find a booking</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>: type at least 3 characters of the booking number (CC-1042, 1042), the renter&#39;s or a driver&#39;s name, an email, a phone number, a plate or a car code, then press Enter. <b class="gd-ui">My bookings</b> lists yours, with your commission. Every search is logged, as Find a renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer for new requests, replies to answer and urgent problems, even with the portal closed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> (top of the menu). Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications. The first page of the portal also offers it once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>: new requests, booking changes and messages are on for staff; payments are off until you tick them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> checks the device. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes an old phone off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>). Use your phone&#39;s own Focus or Do Not Disturb for quiet hours.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Search</h3><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> button at the top of every page (or press <b class="gd-ui">/</b> where the page has no search box of its own) finds pages and the records your role may open: bookings and requests by number, renter name, email, phone or plate, renters, owners and cars.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A VIN from the car</h3><p class="gd-p">VIN fields have <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> (the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or under the windshield) and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Check what was read against the car before saving.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-alerts-by-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alerts by email</h2><p class="gd-p">Alerts that are not urgent come together in one email at most once an hour; urgent ones (a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, the site down) still come on their own. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once. Choose on <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, Notifications: alerts by email, <b class="gd-ui">Change how often</b>: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>To change the email you sign in with, open Profile, Sign-in and press <b class="gd-ui">Change my email</b>: type the new address, and we send a confirmation link to it and tell the old address. Your email changes only when the link is opened, and every record of yours follows it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-my-rewards-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My rewards (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">My rewards</b> is on To do and in the menu under My numbers. It shows your discount, your tier and your free rental days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. If you work remotely or outside Canada, the card says there are no rental perks on your account, because you cannot rent here.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From the day your academy and your agreement are done you get 15% off your own rentals. Your code is on the page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Sales: you earn 1 free rental day for every 100 rental days you book. Book 50 rental days in a month for <b class="gd-ui">Silver</b> (20% off) and 100 for <b class="gd-ui">Gold</b> (25% off and 1 bonus free day that month). A tier lasts through the next month. The month&#39;s top seller gets a free weekend.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">To use free days, press <b class="gd-ui">Get a free-day code</b>, choose how many days, and use the code on one rental. A free day ends 6 months after you earn it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The rules: you must be the driver; not on exotic or partner cars; the pickup is within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter has asked for; free days go on CarmaCars&#39; own cars first.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-choose-your-notifications-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Choose your notifications (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, under <b class="gd-ui">Notification preferences</b>, lists each kind of notification we send you, with a switch for <b class="gd-ui">Push</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. A switch is saved the moment you move it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How often</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Instant</b> sends each one as it happens. <b class="gd-ui">Daily summary</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary</b> holds the optional emails and sends them as one email in the morning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quiet hours</b>: turn them on and set the times. Optional phone alerts and texts wait until the quiet hours end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn every optional notification off</b> stops them all at once. You still see every message in your portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The kinds under <b class="gd-ui">Always on</b> cannot be switched off: security and sign-in codes, agreement notices, pay statements, the work assigned to you, and onboarding, access and suspension notices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">If a text cannot be sent, the same message comes by email instead, so nothing is lost.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'report-rentals-referrals-and-profile', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.

## Report a problem

1. On Today, press **Add**, then **A problem with a car**, and choose the Car.
2. Choose What happened: **New damage found**, **Warning light**, **Collision while I was driving**, **Ticket or toll while I was driving**, **Lost property found** or **Something else**.
3. Write the Details: where, when and what you see.
4. Press **Take a photo** for each photo, then **Send the report**.

![](/guides/img/field-03-report-phone-3b903b20.jpg "phone; size: 390 1040; pins: 1 93.6 46.6, 2 93.6 64.9, 3 93.6 89.9")

> Watch out: In a collision, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if anyone is hurt. Then call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991 before you send the report.

## Add a rental for a renter you found

Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.

1. On the Sales tab (or Profile), open **Add a rental**. Choose the car, the dates and the places, then type the renter''s details. A renter already on file is found by their email. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: it is recorded as on trip.
2. Press **Check the calendar and the price**. To charge another price, type it with the reason: a price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin, not refused.
3. Choose **Send a payment link** or **Charge the saved card when the renter signs**. The renter pays online: you take no payment for it yourself.
4. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**, then press **Add the rental**.

## Commissions

1. You earn 10% of the rental charge (before tax, after discounts, less refunds) of each rental you sourced: one you added and marked I sourced this client, or a booking made with your referral link.
2. It is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, then an Admin approves it and it is paid on your pay date. Your home address must be in your profile: until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet.
3. **My sales** shows each commission: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid or reversed. A refund after payment comes off a later commission.

## Do sales too

On **Profile**, press **I want to do sales too**. The Sales path is added to Training; once you pass it, the **Sales** tab opens with the Sales pages. Your field work goes on as before.

## Referrals and profile

1. **Referrals**: your own referral link. Press **Copy the link**, or let someone scan its QR code. A booking made with it counts as a rental you sourced.
2. **Profile**: **Save my phone**, your home address (**Change my home address**), **Pay details** (how you are paid: only the last 4 digits of an account number are shown again), **Set up two-step sign-in**, **Change my email** (a link goes to the new address and the old one is told), **Change my password** and **Sign out**.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 2 92.3 78.3")

## Sign in with your phone number

Quicker on a phone than a password: a 6-digit code by text.

1. On **Profile**, under Sign-in, press **Add and verify my phone number**, enter your mobile number and press **Text me a code**.
2. Type the code from the text (it usually fills itself in) and press **Verify**. Choose **My phone number (a code by text)** under Sign in with.
3. Next time, the sign-in page opens on your phone number: press **Text me a code** and enter the code. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

## Texts or email

On **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both** for the messages we send you. Texts need the phone you verified above.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert the moment a job is assigned to you or changes, and when you are paid. Open **Profile**, press **Turn on alerts** under **Phone alerts** and allow notifications. On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**) and turn alerts on from there.

## Alerts

The bell at the top opens **Alerts**: your jobs assigned, changed and running late, and urgent alerts passed to you. With phone alerts on (**Alerts** > **Settings**), they reach your phone too, and at 8 am a short brief of your jobs that day. A late job alert has **Mark picked up** (it opens the booking) and **Snooze 30 min**. Quiet hours (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them) hold the ones that are not urgent.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.', 'Report, rentals, referrals and profile', 'Report an incident, add a rental, commissions, your referral link and your profile.',
  'Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.

## Report a problem

1. On Today, press **Add**, then **A problem with a car**, and choose the Car.
2. Choose What happened: **New damage found**, **Warning light**, **Collision while I was driving**, **Ticket or toll while I was driving**, **Lost property found** or **Something else**.
3. Write the Details: where, when and what you see.
4. Press **Take a photo** for each photo, then **Send the report**.

![](/guides/img/field-03-report-phone-3b903b20.jpg "phone; size: 390 1040; pins: 1 93.6 46.6, 2 93.6 64.9, 3 93.6 89.9")

> Watch out: In a collision, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if anyone is hurt. Then call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991 before you send the report.

## Add a rental for a renter you found

Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.

1. On the Sales tab (or Profile), open **Add a rental**. Choose the car, the dates and the places, then type the renter''s details. A renter already on file is found by their email. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: it is recorded as on trip.
2. Press **Check the calendar and the price**. To charge another price, type it with the reason: a price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin, not refused.
3. Choose **Send a payment link** or **Charge the saved card when the renter signs**. The renter pays online: you take no payment for it yourself.
4. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**, then press **Add the rental**.

## Commissions

1. You earn 10% of the rental charge (before tax, after discounts, less refunds) of each rental you sourced: one you added and marked I sourced this client, or a booking made with your referral link.
2. It is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, then an Admin approves it and it is paid on your pay date. Your home address must be in your profile: until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet.
3. **My sales** shows each commission: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid or reversed. A refund after payment comes off a later commission.

## Do sales too

On **Profile**, press **I want to do sales too**. The Sales path is added to Training; once you pass it, the **Sales** tab opens with the Sales pages. Your field work goes on as before.

## Referrals and profile

1. **Referrals**: your own referral link. Press **Copy the link**, or let someone scan its QR code. A booking made with it counts as a rental you sourced.
2. **Profile**: **Save my phone**, your home address (**Change my home address**), **Pay details** (how you are paid: only the last 4 digits of an account number are shown again), **Set up two-step sign-in**, **Change my email** (a link goes to the new address and the old one is told), **Change my password** and **Sign out**.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 2 92.3 78.3")

## Sign in with your phone number

Quicker on a phone than a password: a 6-digit code by text.

1. On **Profile**, under Sign-in, press **Add and verify my phone number**, enter your mobile number and press **Text me a code**.
2. Type the code from the text (it usually fills itself in) and press **Verify**. Choose **My phone number (a code by text)** under Sign in with.
3. Next time, the sign-in page opens on your phone number: press **Text me a code** and enter the code. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

## Texts or email

On **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both** for the messages we send you. Texts need the phone you verified above.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert the moment a job is assigned to you or changes, and when you are paid. Open **Profile**, press **Turn on alerts** under **Phone alerts** and allow notifications. On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**) and turn alerts on from there.

## Alerts

The bell at the top opens **Alerts**: your jobs assigned, changed and running late, and urgent alerts passed to you. With phone alerts on (**Alerts** > **Settings**), they reach your phone too, and at 8 am a short brief of your jobs that day. A late job alert has **Mark picked up** (it opens the booking) and **Snooze 30 min**. Quiet hours (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them) hold the ones that are not urgent.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.

## My rewards (release 48)

1. **My rewards** is on Today and in the menu under Me. It shows your discount on your own rentals and the free rental days you earn.
2. From the day your academy and your agreement are done you get 15% off your own rentals. Your code is on the page: type it in the promo code box when you send a request, signed in as yourself.
3. You earn 1 free rental day for every 100 handovers you complete. The bar shows how many are left. A free day ends 6 months after you earn it.
4. To use free days, press **Get a free-day code**, choose how many days, and use the code on one rental. A code you have not used can be cancelled, and its days come back.
5. The rules: you must be the driver; not on exotic or partner cars; the pickup is within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter has asked for; free days go on CarmaCars'' own cars first. A suspended account''s perks are frozen.

## Choose your notifications (release 48)

1. **Profile**, under **Notification preferences**, lists each kind of notification we send you, with a switch for **Push**, **Email** and **Text**. A switch is saved the moment you move it.
2. **How often**: **Instant** sends each one as it happens. **Daily summary** or **Weekly summary** holds the optional emails and sends them as one email in the morning.
3. **Quiet hours**: turn them on and set the times. Optional phone alerts and texts wait until the quiet hours end.
4. **Turn every optional notification off** stops them all at once. You still see every message in your portal.
5. The kinds under **Always on** cannot be switched off: security and sign-in codes, agreement notices, pay statements, the jobs and shifts assigned to you, and onboarding, access and suspension notices.
6. If a text cannot be sent, the same message comes by email instead, so nothing is lost.
